# MT1 (stream S15-threads) - gated Switch behaviour changes for the engine's multithreaded culling (bMTRendering:
# Display, 0x011c710c), docs/PATCHES.md "Patch class MT1" and docs/PERF.md 6.8. Exempt from the MSVC byte check:
# these hunks change behaviour on purpose, and only when bMTRendering is set; with it 0 every site does what the PC
# code does. Checked by GCC census, mtqemu on the real objects, the race checker and frame equivalence instead.
#
# Design (PERF.md 6.8): only the main-scene split (record 21: the worker culls leftList2 while main culls
# rightList4 / commonList3) runs concurrently. Both threads then write the same accumulator, so it needs a second
# batch renderer for the worker (TLS 0x2bc = 1); every other record runs the engine's own inline path. Water (1-16)
# was signalled and waited at once anyway; the shadow lights (17-20) and the interface record (23) overlapped main
# while main rewrote the current-accumulator globals (DAT_011f95ec, DAT_011f4748+8), and inline they no longer do.
# During record 21 both threads set those globals to the same accumulator (main re-points them just before,
# main.cpp FUN_00b54ac0 / FUN_004dc540 on m_88), and both setters skip an unchanged value, so they stay unwritten.

@@ MT1 src/staging/blk_00860000_od.cpp 0x0086c160
# The main scene's accumulator (m_88, record 21's): two batch renderers when MT culling is on. The ctor
# (bsshaderaccumulator.cpp 0x00b660d0) builds the second one only for count 2; RenderBound picks one by
# tls[0x2bc] % count and AccumulateRenderPasses indexes m_apkRenderers[tls 0x2bc] unchecked, so with count 1 the
# worker would index a NULL renderer. fnvnx_mt1_batches(): shim/include/fnvnx_mt1.h (1 with bMTRendering=0).
<<<
    acc88.FUN_0066b0d0(new BSShaderAccumulator(99, 1, 759));
===
    acc88.FUN_0066b0d0(new BSShaderAccumulator(99, fnvnx_mt1_batches(), 759));
>>>

@@ MT1 src/bsshader/mtrenderingsystem_o2_variant.cpp 0x00ba3390
# Only record 21 is handed to Rendering Task Thread 2; every other record takes the function's own inline path
# (the bMTRendering=0 branch: a BSCullingProcess on the caller's thread). Its record stays empty, so the worker
# (0x00ba3190) skips it and still signals its stage: 0x00ba30f0 / 0x00ba3130 work unchanged.
<<<
    if (::DAT_011f94b4)
    {
        self->GetTask(a8).sp00 = a1;
===
    if (::DAT_011f94b4 && a8 == 21)
    {
        self->GetTask(a8).sp00 = a1;
>>>
